# Observability, logging & tracing anchor

Apply when adding/changing logging, tracing, error diagnostics, HTTP request correlation, SQLx instrumentation, external-call telemetry, Rig telemetry, or production diagnostics.

## Hard invariants

- Use structured `tracing` spans/events rather than isolated string logs.
- Preserve causal request/job/agent-run context across relevant boundaries.
- Do not hold an entered span guard across `.await`; use async-safe instrumentation.
- Log an error at the operationally meaningful boundary instead of duplicating it at every layer.
- Preserve error chains internally.
- Runtime filtering must allow targeted local debugging without recompilation.
- Secrets and sensitive payloads are not normal telemetry.
- High-cardinality identifiers belong in trace/log fields, not blindly in metric labels.

